      "writtenOn": "2020-05-29T01:52:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please see 6-49 Chunked Message Router State Diagram.\n\nThe problem is when we receive a message before a pending tx message is processed by TCH_WAIT_FOR_MESSAGE_REQUEST_FROM_PE. By checking the PRL_FLAGS_MSG_XMIT flag, the RTR state machine can navigate to the proper state.\n\nFor example:\n(normal case):\n  1) call pe_send_msg. This sets PRL_FLAGS_MSG_XMIT\n  2) TCH_WAIT_FOR_MESSAGE_REQUEST_FROM_PE transition to some other state\n  3) We receive a message.\n  4) The RTR_WAIT_FOR_MESSAGE_FROM_PROTOCOL_LAYER transitions to RTR_TX_CHUNKS\n  \n(edge case):\n  1) call pe_send_msg. This sets PRL_FLAGS_MSG_XMIT\n  2) We receive a message.\n  3) The RTR_WAIT_FOR_MESSAGE_FROM_PROTOCOL_LAYER transitions to RTR_RX_CHUNKS\n  4) TCH_WAIT_FOR_MESSAGE_REQUEST_FROM_PE transition to some other state",
      "parentUuid": "445a45e9_10712400",
